HP's Calendar (com.palm.app.calendar), as modernized by webOS Archive for webOS Community
Edition: version 3.2.0, "Calendar (webOS CE)", from the WOSA Modernize feed
(com.palm.app.calendar_3.2.0_all.ipk), built from the webOS CE project's tree. It opens on a
calendar kept on the device ("On This Device") instead of asking for an HP account, and keeps
that calendar when the account it belongs to is replaced, and its half-hour dividers reach the
edge of a screen wider than the TouchPad's, and saving an event no longer scrolls the day back
to midnight.

The original is copyright Palm, Inc. / Hewlett-Packard, never released under an open licence;
distributed by Lunacy as abandonware, like Mojo, the Prelude fonts and the TouchPad wallpapers:
no owner has asserted rights since webOS was discontinued. The 3.2.0 changes are webOS
Archive's.

Import Calendar in the App Menu is webOS CE's (webos-doctor-ce commits ed32d2b to 6eae747; the
tree stays at 3.2.0, so look for app/import/). app/import/webcal/ is from webos-webcal-synergy,
licensed under the GNU GPL version 3 (app/import/webcal/LICENSE.txt), approved by codepoet for
Calendar. Its four .js files stay identical to that repository.

The app's files are here exactly as the package carries them, and Lunacy does not change them
(rule 5 in CLAUDE.md). A change Lunacy needs in the app is made in the webOS CE project and
comes here with its next release.
